{"title":"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be the right-angled isosceles triangle whose equal sides have length 1. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a point on the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hypotenuse\" title=\"Hypotenuse\">hypotenuse</a>, and the feet of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendiculars</a> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the other sides are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Consider the areas of the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/0/880518fa90ebed1440cedcc1a86d052a01c4b434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/6/636defc88bf9618a149d99dd3d03c0b2f82531b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PBR$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, and the area of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangle</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/7/9d79f8a3e23a4acdac26ec613453bd8f0dfce255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QCRP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" />. Prove that regardless of how <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen, the largest of these three areas is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/4/3f4d572697ba6b0bedff704766358ae7b39d95a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2/9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caa9f7cf2a02576793da21a0a40b18195ad87548.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ=x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" /> Because <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangles</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/0/880518fa90ebed1440cedcc1a86d052a01c4b434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/5/655e115e19078e6410111d99ee046f4a3d4509de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BPR$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> both contain a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_angle\" title=\"Right angle\">right angle</a> and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8adb649f063149ebc97d3ee58c4fd38d4c440846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> angle, they are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isosceles_triangle\" title=\"Isosceles triangle\"> isosceles</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right triangles</a>. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/8/dc875d550cc1ea4241389988330912dc5e001cf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ=RC=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5fdc37f060ff86fbd73bb3e2b1f9ad945249b26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QC=PR=BR=1-x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"203\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Now let's consider when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e9373635badc92e52e0cfe6775d742d375eb3443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac13 &lt;x&lt;\\frac23,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"89\" height=\"37\" /> or else one of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/0/880518fa90ebed1440cedcc1a86d052a01c4b434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/6/636defc88bf9618a149d99dd3d03c0b2f82531b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PBR$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> will automatically have area greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/763f1814f0201699503c50d718c4155fdab49bf7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac29.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"16\" height=\"37\" /> In this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/4/cb4a872a38efb537903488e5ddb5c83f5f40f1b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[QCRP] = [ABC]-[APQ]-[PBR]&gt;\\frac29.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"334\" height=\"37\" /> Therefore, one of these three figures will always have area greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/7/5178002b597b6c74dd8f95d6e65ca3bcd9e9f908.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac29,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"17\" height=\"37\" /> regardless of where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO\">1969 Canadian MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last question</b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016222447\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 125/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 985/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 67/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3979/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.290      1 Template:Old_CanadaMO_box\n100.00%   11.290      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3616:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016222447 and revision id 74105. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}